  "answer": "The test uses `bun:test`. Let me run the existing test to confirm the failure first.\nTest fails as expected. Now I'll repair `src/tokens.ts` — trim each comma-separated token and omit empty ones, keeping the signature `tokens(value: string)` unchanged.\nRepair applied. Verifying by running the test again:\nThe repair is verified. Summary:\n\n**Failure confirmed** — `bun test` initially failed: `tokens('')` returned `['']` instead of `[]`, and `tokens(' a, ,b ,,c ')` returned untrimmed tokens with empties.\n\n**Repair** in `src/tokens.ts` (one line, signature preserved):\n\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string) { return value.split(',').map(token => token.trim()).filter(token => token.length > 0) }\n```\n\n- `.map(token => token.trim())` trims whitespace around each comma-separated token\n- `.filter(token => token.length > 0)` omits empty tokens (this also makes `tokens('')` return `[]`, since `['']` is filtered out)\n- The function signature `tokens(value: string)` and its `string[]` return type are unchanged\n\n**Verification** — `bun test` now passes: 1 test, 3 assertions, 0 failures. The test file `test/oracle.test.ts` was left untouched."
